          "question": "I think maybe something is wrong with my chest. It feels like someone heavy is sitting on it and it started about twenty minutes ago.",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now. Do not wait to see whether the pressure passes.**\n\nHeavy pressure in the centre of the chest that lasts more than a few minutes is treated as a possible heart attack until proven otherwise. That comes from the red-flag chest pain guidance (*Chest pain that may indicate a heart attack*, emergency medicine and cardiology society guidance). Your symptom has lasted about 20 minutes, so it fits that pattern.\n\nThe urgency tool returned \"routine\" because its fixed table did not match your exact words. That result does not mean the symptom is minor. I am rating this as an emergency because the guidance above is clear on this pattern.\n\nTell the emergency team right away if you also have any of these, which the same guidance lists as warning signs:\n- Pain or discomfort spreading to the arms, shoulders, neck, jaw, back or upper stomach\n- Breathlessness, cold sweat, nausea or vomiting, or light-headedness\n- A sense of impending doom\n\nIf you have a known heart condition or diabetes, the guidance treats any chest discomfort as urgent.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
